# The IPC benchmark's medians (user/ipcbench, CPU cycles by its ruler) as
# measured on 2026-10-14 on the P53's Intel Core i7-9850H, through KVM in
# QEMU 10.0.13 inside the build VM (8 vCPUs), with nothing else running there:
# 20 runs of the bench-gate entry of test/selftest.sh. (Before that, Phase 3
# step 8, 2026-10-13, on the Intel Core i5-14400: 376, 1356, 764.)
# The two IPC figures are the runs' median (1336-1344 and 876-880 in all 20).
# The system call's median falls in two groups: 336-352 (16 runs) and 444-476
# (4 runs). Its figure here is not that median but the lowest that passes
# both groups (476 <= 384 + 384/4); see docs/phase3-data.
# The gate in test/selftest.sh fails a run whose median is more than 25% above
# these (docs/phase3-plan.md, *Testing*). Change them only with a measurement
# and a reason, recorded in docs/phase3-data.
#
# measurement (the start of the line ipcbench prints) | median
a system call that does nothing|384
two address spaces, passive server|1344
one address space, passive server|880
